---
import DocLayout from '../../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../../lib/site';
---

<DocLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  lead="The rules for using TCG Vault and its marketplace. By using the site you agree to them."
  group="legal"
  updated="5 October 2026"
>
  <p class="doc-note">
    In short: TCG Vault helps collectors find each other and keep track of trades. It is not a shop. Buyers and sellers deal
    with each other directly, and TCG Vault is not a party to their trades.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who runs TCG Vault</h2>
  <p>
    TCG Vault is a free fan project run by a private individual. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Your account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You need to be at least 16 to create an account.</li>
    <li>Use a display name that doesn't impersonate anyone, and keep your password to yourself. You are responsible for what happens on your account.</li>
    <li>One person, one account. Using extra accounts to review yourself, inflate sales or get around a ban is not allowed.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. How the marketplace works</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>A buyer requests a hold on one or more cards and chooses a handover method.</li>
    <li>The seller accepts or rejects the request. Accepting reserves the cards for that buyer.</li>
    <li>The two agree on payment and handover in Messages. TCG Vault does not process payments or hold money.</li>
    <li>The seller marks the cards as handed over (met up or sent).</li>
    <li>The buyer confirms they received them, which completes the sale. If the buyer doesn't respond within 14 days of handover, the seller can complete it.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    See the <a href="/help/shipping">shipping &amp; handover guide</a> and the <a href="/help/selling">seller guidelines</a> for
    the practical side.
  </p>

  <h2>4. If you sell</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Only list cards you own and can hand over. Describe them honestly: the right card, version, finish and condition, with real photos where you add them.</li>
    <li>The price, shipping costs and minimum order you set are what the buyer agrees to; don't add charges afterwards.</li>
    <li>Answer hold requests promptly, and hand over what you agreed to, the way you agreed to.</li>
    <li>Only mark a hold as handed over once you have actually met up or sent the cards.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. If you buy</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Only request holds you intend to complete, and pay as agreed with the seller.</li>
    <li>Confirm you received the cards once you have them, and don't confirm before.</li>
    <li>If something is wrong, talk to the seller first in Messages. If you can't sort it out, email us.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Not allowed</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Counterfeit or proxy cards sold as real, and anything you don't own.</li>
    <li>Scams, fake listings, payment fraud, or using the site to move money for others.</li>
    <li>Harassment, threats, hate speech, or spam in messages, reviews or profiles.</li>
    <li>Fake or traded reviews, and reviews used to pressure the other person.</li>
    <li>Scraping the site, overloading it, or trying to get into accounts or data that aren't yours.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Reviews</h2>
  <p>
    After a completed trade, each side can rate the other once. Reviews should describe that trade honestly. We may remove
    reviews that break these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your content</h2>
  <p>
    You keep the rights to the photos and text you post. By posting them you let TCG Vault show them on the site for as long
    as they are up. Don't post anything you don't have the right to share.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Prices and card data</h2>
  <p>
    Market prices and estimated values are approximate and for reference only. Card information comes from public sources
    and may contain mistakes.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Suspension and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    We may hide listings, remove content, or suspend or delete accounts that break these terms or put other users at risk.
    You can ask us to delete your account at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>11. No guarantees</h2>
  <p>
    TCG Vault is provided as it is, for free. We do our best to keep it running and your data safe, but we can't promise it
    will always be available or error-free. We are not responsible for trades between users, including payments, deliveries,
    the condition of cards, or losses that come from them, except where the law says we must be.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes and governing law</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms; the date at the top shows the latest version, and we will mention important changes on the site.
    These terms are governed by Hungarian law. Nothing here takes away rights you have as a consumer where you live.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
